# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The Dockerfile uses explicit COPY paths rather than "COPY . .", so this file
# governs what the builder transfers and hashes on every build rather than what
# lands in the image. Keeping it tight still matters: the context is synced on
# each build -- and UPLOADED to Azure by "az acr build" -- while "app/build"
# alone is ~50 MB of jars.
#
# NOTE: do NOT add any of these -- the build breaks without them:
#   gradlew, gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar, settings.gradle.kts,
#   gradle.properties, app/gradle.properties, app/build.gradle.kts,
#   .editorconfig (spotless reads it), all three *.lockfile files, and
#   app/src/test (bootJar depends on check, which runs the suite).

# ---------- Gradle output and caches ----------
# Rebuilt inside the image; machine-specific and large.
build/
app/build/
# ...except the Spring Boot layered jar that the builder stage copies. Docker
# applies the LAST matching pattern, so this re-admits that single file while
# app/build/ keeps out the ~50 MB of versioned, sources and javadoc jars
# beside it. The name is fixed -- the "applicationJar" Gradle task renames the
# versioned bootJar -- so this pattern does not churn with the version.
!app/build/libs/spring-blueprint-spring-boot.jar
.gradle/
app/.gradle/

# ---------- Git metadata ----------
# Verified safe to exclude: ":app:bootJar" was run against a copy of this
# repository with no .git directory and succeeded. The release plugin touches
# git only when the "release" task runs, which a container build never does.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ---------- IDE and OS ----------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/
bin/
.DS_Store

# ---------- Docs and repo furniture ----------
# Not needed to compile or test.
*.md
LICENSE
llms.txt
misc/
commands/
.github/

# ---------- Local credentials ----------
# GitHub Packages auth is supplied as build args, never through the context.
.env
*.env
.secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# ---------- Docker's own files ----------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# ---------- CI tooling ----------
# An ACR Tasks task definition, not an input to the image build. The deploy
# workflow reads it from $RUNNER_TEMP, not from the context.
acr-smoke-test.yaml
